    {
        "content": "<p>I've been thinking about adding constructible numbers to Mathlib (primarily so we can get results proving impossibility to trisect an angle or double the cube). The structure I'm thinking of is as follows:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The field of numbers we'll work in is <code>ℂ</code> and we'd show that by taking real part, imaginary part, or norm, that we'd get real constructible numbers.</li>\n<li>Define Geometric constructible numbers as the set of points which can be generated by intersections of distinct lines or circles.</li>\n<li>Define Algebraic constructible numbers as the subfield of <code>ℂ</code> generated by <code>0</code>, <code>1</code> and closed under field operations and sqrt. </li>\n<li>Prove geometric constructible numbers are equivalent to algebraic constructible numbers.</li>\n<li>Prove any constructible number has degree a power of 2, and therefore conclude impossibility to trisect a general angle or doubling the cube.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Thus far I've only tried coming up with some definitions:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- `z` lies on the line through `a` and `b`.-/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OnLine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">line</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- `z` lies on the circle centred at `c` whose radius is the distance from `p` to `q`.-/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OnCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- `z` is constructible by straightedge and compass from the points `0` and `1`. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The intersection point of two distinct lines through constructible points. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lineLine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">OnLine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OnLine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">-- the two lines are genuinely different</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">OnLine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OnLine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- An intersection point of a line and a circle through constructible points. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lineCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">OnLine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OnCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- An intersection point of two circles with distinct constructible centres. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">circleCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"c1\">-- distinct centres; concentric circles either coincide or do not meet</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">OnCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OnCircle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IsConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- `z` lies in the smallest subfield of `ℂ` that is closed under taking square roots. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">neg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsAlgConstructible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, I'm not sure what we'd actually want for the geometric definition of constructible numbers. In particular, would we want the definition to enforce a collapsible compass (so <code>p = c</code> above, or instead the main API use a non-collapsible compass, and we prove the equivalence between the two? I want to stick to the latter, primarily because its a lot easier to use. </p>\n<p>Additionally, I've inducted up from <code>0</code>, <code>1</code>, but perhaps we'd want to start with an arbitrary set of complex points and build it up from there? Alternatively, we could induct the <code>0</code>, <code>1</code> case up for a general set of points. This could lead to more general proofs, but not sure if we want to support that immediately. </p>\n<p>Let me know if you have any ideas! I'll keep working via this API to see how difficult it is to prove the geometric-algebraic equivalency for the time being.</p>",
        "id": 615634878,
        "sender_full_name": "Sharvil Kesarwani",
        "timestamp": 1786371350
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have my version of constructible numbers and points at <a href=\"https://github.com/wwylele/Compass\">https://github.com/wwylele/Compass</a> and it is linked in 100.yml in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41757\">#41757</a> that has just merged. I might upstream it in the future, but happy to collab on this (busy rn. Will take further look at yours later)</p>",
        "id": 615640390,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1786372809
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>we could generalize this to the relative quadratic closure of one field inside another</p>",
        "id": 615640430,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786372816
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wow nice job <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"873350\">@Weiyi Wang</span> , this is in far more generality than I had, and it even has the relative quadratic closure <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816344\">@Aaron Liu</span> mentions! I'd be happy with helping upstream this. Longer term, I do see it being able to support Mohr–Mascheroni and Poncelet–Steiner, and an origami (Huzita–Hatori) axiom set would be a nice counterpoint since trisection becomes possible there. Not proposing any of those now though, but it feels like these would be in reach once we have this in.</p>",
        "id": 615648058,
        "sender_full_name": "Sharvil Kesarwani",
        "timestamp": 1786374582
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think what you listed is indeed mostly what I followed in my repo, with generalizations</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The relative quadratic closure between any fields, which I (mis)named as <code>constructibleClosure</code>. I defined it using the iterated quadratic extension, and stated the add/neg/mul/inv/sqrt construction as induction principles.</li>\n<li><code>ConstructiblePoint</code> is on any Euclidean affine plane. <code>ℂ</code> is an Euclidean affine plane so it applies directly. I also allowed an arbitrary set of starting points.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I allowed collapsible compass in my construction, though I don't know whether that is more preferred by the community.</p>",
        "id": 615737597,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1786406713
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I had a go with using my rigid compass definition to build up the collapsible equivalency, and proving equivalency to algebraic closure. It feels like rigid is more flexible at the introduction site (setting a circle's radius from any two constructible points makes constructions shorter). Collapsible gives a sharper induction principle, fewer points per case. </p>\n<p>Points for collapsible:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>rigid just assumes Euclid I.2 in the definition rather than proving it</li>\n<li><code>centerRadius'</code> already gives us the rigid tool in your writeup so nothing downstream should be harder</li>\n<li>we'd need to prove rigid =&gt; collapsible anyways</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I think collapsible might be the right approach.</p>",
        "id": 615841328,
        "sender_full_name": "Sharvil Kesarwani",
        "timestamp": 1786451825
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For upstreaming, we can probably begin with getting <code>ConstructibleNumber.lean</code> up, that seems to be independent of any other file in your repo. We can also probably do another independent PR for <code>ConstructiblePoint.lean</code>.</p>",
        "id": 615848922,
        "sender_full_name": "Sharvil Kesarwani",
        "timestamp": 1786453958
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah for constructible numbers, I started with some small PR like <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41905\">#41905</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42044\">#42044</a>.</p>",
        "id": 615849574,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1786454145
    }
]